---
# NOTE: `Checks:` below is a YAML folded scalar -- everything indented under it
# is literal text, so a `#` line inside it is NOT a comment.  It gets folded
# into the check-name string and silently swallows the neighbouring entries,
# which clang-tidy accepts without a word.  Keep rationale here, above the key.
#
# Rationale for the non-obvious entries:
#
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
#     Byte sizes here are routinely width * height * bpp.  misplaced-widening-cast
#     only catches a cast applied too late; this catches the 32-bit multiply that
#     overflows before any widening happens, which is how an undersized staging
#     allocation turns into an out-of-bounds copy.
#
#   concurrency-mt-unsafe (FunctionSet: posix)
#     Re-enabled after being dropped as noise.  That call was wrong: the one
#     finding that survived was a real std::localtime data race in the native
#     build (process-global struct tm plus a lazy tzset), together with an
#     unchecked null return fed straight into strftime.  The noise came from the
#     default 'any' function set flagging single-threaded init code; 'posix'
#     keeps the reentrancy signal without it.
#
#   -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#     Annex K (fprintf_s and friends) is not implemented by the macOS libc, so
#     every diagnostic this sub-check emits is unfixable by construction.  It was
#     only ever pulled in by the security.* wildcard, and it produced the entire
#     deep baseline -- 55 entries whose counts had to be bumped each time anyone
#     added a diagnostic fprintf.  A check that can only be baselined is noise.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-assert-side-effect,
  bugprone-dangling-handle,
  bugprone-exception-escape,
  bugprone-infinite-loop,
  bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast,
  bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  bugprone-multiple-statement-macro,
  bugprone-sizeof-container,
  bugprone-sizeof-expression,
  bugprone-suspicious-memset-usage,
  bugprone-unused-raii,
  bugprone-use-after-move,
  bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  bugprone-integer-division,
  bugprone-too-small-loop-variable,
  bugprone-signed-char-misuse,
  bugprone-inc-dec-in-conditions,
  misc-no-recursion,
  concurrency-mt-unsafe,
  clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.UninitializedObject,
  clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.VirtualCall,
  clang-analyzer-core.*,
  clang-analyzer-cplusplus.*,
  clang-analyzer-deadcode.*,
  clang-analyzer-nullability.*,
  clang-analyzer-osx.cocoa.RetainCount,
  clang-analyzer-security.*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  clang-analyzer-unix.Malloc,
  clang-analyzer-unix.MismatchedDeallocator,
  clang-analyzer-unix.cstring.*,
  performance-noexcept-move-constructor
CheckOptions:
  concurrency-mt-unsafe.FunctionSet: posix
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '(^|/)(include|src)/(d3d12|dxmt|winemetal4)/'
SystemHeaders: false
FormatStyle: none
...
